{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GPYBEJjoNoxbe3DarSaJ5K","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Differential Testing Framework - Complete Analysis\n\n### 1. DiffTest Struct (pkg/testutils/difftest.go)\n\n**Full struct definition with all field names, types, and purposes:**\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string              // Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run)\n\tArgs          []string            // Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n\tStdin         []byte              // Input to both binaries (nil = EOF immediately, []byte{} = open stdin immediately closed)\n\tEnv           []string            // Environment variables; nil inherits test process env with LC_ALL=C; non-nil entries override/add to inherited env\n\tWorkDir       string              // Working directory for test; if empty, a temp directory is created\n\tExitCode      int                 // Expected exit code (defaults to 0 when zero value)\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc     // Slice of normalization functions applied in order to stdout and stderr before comparison\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte   // Map of relative file paths to expected file contents (for verifying filesystem modifications)\n}\n```\n\n**Field names in order:**\n- Name\n- Args\n- Stdin\n- Env\n- WorkDir\n- ExitCode\n- Normalize\n- ExpectedFiles\n\n### 2. RunDiffTests Function Signature (pkg/testutils/difftest.go, lines 83-90)\n\n```go\n// RunDiffTests runs each DiffTest as a named subtest, executing goBinary and\n// refBinary with identical inputs and comparing their outputs.\n// R2.1: accepts paths to Go and reference binaries plus test cases.\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tfor _, tc := range tests {\n\t\tt.Run(tc.Name, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\trunSubtest(t, goBinary, refBinary, tc)\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n**Signature:** `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)`\n\n### 3. BuildBinary Function Signature (pkg/testutils/build.go, lines 16-27)\n\n```go\n// BuildBinary compiles the Go package at dir and returns the path to the\n// compiled binary. The binary is placed in a temporary directory that is\n// cleaned up when the test completes.\n// R4: compile within the Go module, return binary path, fatal on failure.\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tname := resolvePackageName(dir)\n\ttmpDir := t.TempDir()\n\tbinPath := filepath.Join(tmpDir, name)\n\tcmd := exec.Command(\"go\", \"build\", \"-o\", binPath, dir)\n\toutput, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"BuildBinary: go build %s failed: %v\\n%s\", dir, err, output)\n\t}\n\treturn binPath\n}\n```\n\n**Signature:** `BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string`\n\n### 4. Example Test Pattern from cat_test.go (cmd/cat/cat_test.go)\n\nBasic differential test pattern with stdin:\n```go\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gcat\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary gcat not found\")\n\t}\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t{Name: \"default_stdin\", Stdin: []byte(\"hello\\nworld\\n\")},\n\t\t{Name: \"stdin_dash\", Args: []string{\"-\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"from stdin\\n\")},\n\t\t{Name: \"number_all_n\", Args: []string{\"-n\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"alpha\\n\\nbeta\\n\")},\n\t\t// ... more tests\n\t}\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\nFile-based test pattern:\n```go\nfunc TestDiffFiles(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gcat\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary gcat not found\")\n\t}\n\tdir := t.TempDir()\n\twriteFixture(t, dir, \"file1.txt\", \"aaa\\n\")\n\twriteFixture(t, dir, \"file2.txt\", \"bbb\\n\")\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t{Name: \"multi_file\", Args: []string{\"file1.txt\", \"file2.txt\"}, WorkDir: dir},\n\t}\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Example Test Pattern with ExpectedFiles (cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go)\n\nFilesystem-modifying test pattern showing output file verification:\n```go\n{\n\tName:    \"r1_3_output_file\",\n\tArgs:    []string{\"dups.txt\", \"out.txt\"},\n\tWorkDir: dir,\n\tEnv:     env,\n\tExpectedFiles: map[string][]byte{\n\t\t\"out.txt\": []byte(\"a\\nb\\na\\n\"),\n\t},\n},\n```\n\nThe framework:\n1. Builds the test binary using `BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n2. Runs test cases through `RunDiffTests()` that execute both the Go implementation and reference binary (gcat, guniq, etc.) with identical inputs\n3. Compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes\n4. Supports normalization functions to handle environment-specific output variations\n5. Supports WorkDir for file-based tests and ExpectedFiles to verify that filesystem modifications match reference behavior\n6. Executes each test case in isolation with a default 10-second timeout"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1fbdf482-3838-404f-ba08-a7431c5e1370","uuid":"cfd7057f-133a-48e7-a37f-7e9491a77423","timestamp":"2026-05-20T11:42:55.185Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the differential testing framework in this Go project. Find and read:\n\n1. The DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function signature in pkg/testutils/ — I need the exact fields of DiffTest and how RunDiffTests is called.\n2. An example test file from any cmd/ directory (e.g., cmd/cat/cat_test.go or cmd/sort/sort_test.go) to see the differential testing pattern in practice, especially how backup-related or filesystem-modifying tests are set up.\n3. The BuildBinary function signature in pkg/testutils/.\n\nRead the full files — I need exact struct field names, types, and function signatures. Report all field names of DiffTest verbatim.","agentId":"a56f997e9359e1db6","agentType":"